  "file": "File:Stone plate Enmahgalanna BM 118555.jpg",
  "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
  "artist": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Zunkir\" title=\"User:Zunkir\">Zunkir</a>",
  "description": "Shallow wide circular stone plate or offering-stand (?). Carved from grey stone with polished surface, restored from sherds.. Inscription on the exterior, with the name and title of Enmahgalanna, sister of king Amar-Sîn of Ur III (ca 2046-2038 BC) and high priestress of the Moon god Nanna in his sanctuary of Ur. Also carrying a pictogram of crescent moon. British Museum ME 118555 <a rel=\"nofollow\"",
  "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AStone_plate_Enmahgalanna_BM_118555.jpg",
